ores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 45,4 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 3,7, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,0 a 4,6. En diciembre se adjudicó el 11 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 5 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 123 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.950 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La cantidad de contratos cerca del límite no indica que se hayan violado normas. Puede deberse a presupuestos cerrados o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 169 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 45.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.0 to 4.6. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 123 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,950 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the large number of different awardees show patterns, but do not prove misconduct. Statistical trends can reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not necessarily improper actions.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for consistency in pricing and compare them to other contracts for the same service. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service or are for different needs. Contract [1] could indicate a pattern if others share similar terms.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["ONlFl9NKs6keIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D","4esN3c76mIVLAIVZdUs8KA%3D%3D","eWu3ozRXC6LVGIpKDxgsAQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}